CHAOS CRAFT POUCH
-----------------
A compact, persistent source of crafting materials for Chaos characters.
The pouch is a real item, but it does not contain a pile of individual
material objects. It keeps a durable scoreboard of the materials you have
collected and the materials you have supplied to Chaos crafting actions.

This help page describes the pouch only. Ordinary characters and ordinary
crafting keep their normal rules when no active Chaos craft pouch is present.


GETTING THE POUCH
-----------------
A new Chaos character receives one pouch in the starter bag when the server's
Chaos starter-material feature is enabled. The grant is made at character
creation; existing characters are not retroactively given a pouch.

The pouch can be:

  - carried directly in your inventory;
  - inside a container that you are carrying; or
  - attached to one of your first three belt-attachment slots.

Put it somewhere in that accessible path before using it as a material source.
If it is in a room, in a locker, or outside the carried/belt path, it is not an
active source for your commands.


LOOKING AT THE SCOREBOARD
-------------------------
Use either command:

    look in pouch
    examine pouch

The display lists only entries with a non-zero history. It shows generated and
collected totals, sorts the most-used entries first, and prints the material
VNUM in brackets so a particular tier can be identified without guessing.
The catalog covers:

  salvage materials     400000 through 400209
  encrust jewels         400291 through 400299

The name beside each VNUM is the actual material description. A reboot does
not erase the scoreboard: the pouch and its ledger are persisted with your
character's items.

The pouch is a ledger, not a normal storage bag. You will not find one object
for every line on the scoreboard, and there is no material object to retrieve
from inside it after a count has been recorded.


COLLECTING MATERIALS
--------------------
Place a supported physical material into the pouch with the normal put
commands:

    put <material> pouch
    put all pouch
    put all.<keyword> pouch

Only supported salvage or encrust-material VNUMs are accepted. The physical
material is recorded and removed as part of the collection operation; the
pouch itself is not consumed. An aggregate collection reports how many
materials were recorded after the durable ownership operation completes.

The pouch does not accept coins, unrelated objects, another pouch, or an
unsupported item. If nothing selected is a supported material, the command
leaves your inventory and the scoreboard unchanged.

Collection is durable. If an ownership operation cannot be committed, the
runtime attempts to roll the scoreboard back and retain the material. If that
rollback also fails, the pouch reports that state and asks you to contact
staff; do not repeat a failed collection until its result is clear.


CRAFTING AND FORGING
--------------------
When the active pouch is accessible, its material reserve supplies the raw
material requirements for the normal crafting and forging commands:

    craft ...
    forge ...

The pouch is a non-consuming source. It does not replace the normal tool,
recipe, skill, level, magical-essence, fee, output, or ownership requirements.
Those checks still apply, and a failed craft or forge does not make the pouch
vanish.

Material use is reflected in the scoreboard as generated history. The
collected history remains visible separately, so the page can show both what
was put into the pouch and what the pouch has supplied to crafting.


ENHANCEMENT
-----------
The legacy two-argument enhancement form can use the pouch as its universal
material donor:

    enhance <item> pouch

The pouch is not consumed. The normal enhancement replacement, cost, level,
conflicting-affect, and item eligibility rules still apply. The pouch is a
material source, not a valid enhancement target and not a general-purpose
donor when it was not the material explicitly requested.

Newer aggregate enhancement paths also use the pouch only where the command
asks for its material supply. They do not turn the pouch into an item whose
individual statistics can be inspected or altered.


ENCRUSTING
----------
If you have the encrust skill and an eligible item, the pouch can provide a
virtual encrust jewel by VNUM:

    encrust <item> <jewel-vnum>

The accepted jewel range is 400291 through 400299. The selected jewel is a
temporary material for that operation; no physical jewel has to be carried,
and the pouch remains in place. Normal encrust restrictions still apply,
including the item's type, repairability, artifact status, prior encrusting,
skill, and any other command-specific checks.

The pouch itself cannot be encrusted. It is a source, not an encrust target.


RESTRICTIONS AND TROUBLESHOOTING
--------------------------------
The Chaos craft pouch:

  - cannot be salvaged;
  - cannot receive coins or unsupported objects;
  - cannot be used as the item being enhanced or encrusted;
  - does not increase normal transfer limits or create a material satchel
    chain; and
  - supplies material only while Chaos mode and the starter-material feature
    are active.

If a command cannot find the pouch, check that it is carried directly, nested
under a carried container, or attached to belt slot 1, 2, or 3. If a collection
fails, verify that the object is one of the supported catalog VNUMs and wait
for the command's durable-operation result before trying again.

If the pouch is absent or the server has disabled the Chaos starter-material
feature, legacy inventory-material behavior is unchanged. The pouch never
changes the individual statistics of an item merely by being present; it only
supplies eligible material requirements to commands that already pass their
normal rules.
